    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><dateline><date when="1950-03-11">March 11,
                        1950</date></dateline><salute>Dear <rs type="person"
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__5368">Professor Merritt</rs>:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>Thank you very much for <rs ref="L11322" type="letter">your letter</rs>. I am
                    glad to give you the permission to produce a translation of <rs type="work"
                        ref="#tillich__4CS7I922">THE SHAKING OF THE FOUNDATIONS</rs>. As you see
                    from the enclosed letter from <rs type="person">Prof. Kan</rs><note type="ea"
                        >Liegt nicht vor.</note> I have shown him <rs ref="L11322" type="letter"
                        >your letter</rs> and I agree with his desire to arrange the translation
                    procedure together with <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__5369" type="person">Mr.
                        Goto</rs>.</p>
                <p>It is a great honor for me that <supplied>you</supplied> think my books are worth
                    to be translated into Japanese and will find public there.</p>
                <closer><salute>With all good wishes,<lb/>Sincerely yours,</salute><signed><rs
                            type="person" ref="#tillich_person_id__1928">Prof. Paul
                        Tillich</rs></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
